# The Syracuse (odd-to-odd) window alphabet: time arcs plus numerical order

Universe: all odd x < 2^22; S(x) = (3x+1)/2^v2(3x+1); windows (x, Sx, ..., S^(m-1) x).

## A. m = 4, gauge DESC (order arcs from the larger to the smaller value)

| class | count | frequency | Haar prediction |
|---|---|---|---|
| TT4 | 720845 | 0.343734 | 11/32 = 0.343750 |
| IN (C3 over sink) | 327680 | 0.156254 | 5/32 = 0.156250 |
| OUT (source over C3) | 327679 | 0.156253 | 5/32 = 0.156250 |
| STRONG | 720896 | 0.343759 | 11/32 = 0.343750 |

degenerate windows (a repeated value, the orbit reaches 1 inside the window): 52, first ones [1, 3, 5, 13, 21, 53, 85, 113]
exceptions to the B2 law table(a,b): 0 -> []

Marked vertices (score of the past x, score of the present S^3 x) per class:
  TT4                    {(3, 0): 720845}
  IN (C3 over sink)      {(2, 0): 327680}
  OUT (source over C3)   {(3, 1): 327679}
  STRONG                 {(1, 2): 655360, (2, 1): 65536}

## B. m = 4, gauge ASC (order arcs from the smaller to the larger value)

  TT4                    655360
  IN (C3 over sink)      0
  OUT (source over C3)   0
  STRONG                 1441740
exceptions to the law (TT4 iff a1+a2+a3 <= 4, else STRONG): 0 -> []

## D. Time reversal of the window (same gauge DESC)

  TT4                    -> {'STRONG': 720845}
  IN (C3 over sink)      -> {'STRONG': 327680}
  OUT (source over C3)   -> {'STRONG': 327679}
  STRONG                 -> {'TT4': 655360, 'STRONG': 65536}
Exact identity (asserted for every window): the time-reversed window read with the same gauge is the
converse of the original window read with the opposite gauge; so under DESC it is TT4 iff a1+a2+a3 <= 4
and STRONG otherwise (pure time reversal is not an involution of the DESC alphabet). The converse of the
DESC reading (= negation o time reversal, Redei note) exchanges the two vortices: the a <-> b swap of B2.

## C. Haar law from the valuation word (a_i i.i.d., P(a = k) = 2^-k), generic comparisons

m = 4 DESC: IN (C3 over sink) 5/32, OUT (source over C3) 5/32, STRONG 11/32, TT4 11/32
m = 4 ASC : STRONG 11/16, TT4 5/16
Census deviation at 2^22: TT4 -1.58e-05, IN (C3 over sink) +3.87e-06, OUT (source over C3) +3.40e-06, STRONG +8.52e-06

